{"resourceIdentifier":"1674","resourceName":"Gilé National Reserve REDD Project","description":"The GNR REDD Project is a REDD project, developed in the buffer zone of the Gilé National Reserve in Mozambique, Zambezia Province. The GNR is managed by the ANAC (Administração Nacional das Areas de Conservação – the national public agency responsible for the management of protected areas), which is therefore the project proponent. Since 2007, the Foundation IGF, which is partly financed by the FFEM, is supporting the ANAC to improve the management of the Reserve. The project area is composed of the forests of the buffer zone of the GNR. It was composed of 124 145 ha of Miombo forest in 2010, just before project start date (01-01-2012). Agricultural activities are leading to a mean historical deforestation level of 2 877 ha/yr (0.65 %/yr) in the reference region of the project, between 2000 and 2010. This rate is equivalent to a level of 810 ha/yr in the project area.  The objective is to reduce deforestation by 30% against the reference level in the first 5 years of project implementation and by 70% after 10 years mainly thanks to the support of communities for agricultural activities.","location":{"latitude":-16.539947,"longitude":38.276744},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":null,"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1674"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Zambezia province"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"National Mozambican Public Agency for Parks and Reserves Conservation (ANAC)"},{"type":"string","value":"Mozambique, Mozambique"},{"type":"string","value":"http://www.anac.gov.mz/"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Late to verify"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"68821"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values"